  postButton: {fileID: 1646383753}
  postBlockedReasonText: {fileID: 2111820077}
  shareButtonLabel: {fileID: 1802427391}
  shareButtonLabel2: {fileID: 351559376}
  starEntry:
    ID: BerkelySquare_51.5091_-0.1447
    User: BerkelySquare
    UserName: 
    Latitude: 51.5091
    Longitude: -0.1447
    Title: The Little Creeper
    Content: "Jonathan Moore was not a superstitious man. A historian by trade, he
      had spent years dismantling the ghost stories that gripped London\u2019s oldest
      streets. But there was one house\u201450 Berkeley Square\u2014that refused
      to be explained away. The newspapers called it The Most Haunted House in London.
      The locals avoided it, claiming they had seen something moving in its upper
      windows at night.\nIt was curiosity, not fear, that drove Jonathan to push
      open the rotting door on a fog-heavy October evening. The interior smelled
      of mildew and dust, the walls streaked with something dark and unidentifiable.
      His breath clouded in the cold air, and his footsteps echoed unnaturally. The
      gas lamps had long since been removed, leaving the house in a state of perpetual
      dusk. As he moved deeper inside, the silence pressed in on him like a living
      thing.\nThen came the sound. A faint, wet scuttling from the floor above.\nJonathan
      swallowed hard, forcing himself to climb the decaying staircase. The second
      floor was worse\u2014black mold crawled along the ceiling, and the air was
      thick with rot. The scuttling sound grew louder, now joined by something else\u2014a
      whisper, a voice that barely touched the edge of hearing.\nThen he saw it.\nAt
      the end of the hallway, where the shadows were deepest, something moved. Small,
      hunched, no taller than a child. It crawled toward him on all fours, its limbs
      too long, its fingers scraping the wood. Its face\u2014if it had one\u2014was
      obscured by darkness, save for two eyes, round and bulging, reflecting the
      dim light like a rat's.\nJonathan couldn\u2019t move.\nThe Little Creeper shuddered
      and cocked its head. Then, with an inhuman burst of speed, it rushed him.\nThe
      next morning, a constable passing the house noticed the front door ajar. He
      found Jonathan's notebook discarded in the hallway, its final page covered
      in frantic scrawl:\n\"It sees me.\"\nBut Jonathan himself was never seen again."
    Theme: Spooky
